        "original_id": "4596c7b8-7d1f-56fe-9175-7b25c37dea59",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Minardi M190, Minardi M189B, Cosworth DFR V8 engine, Pirelli tyres\n- Companies: Pirelli & C. S.p.A., ChemChina, Pirelli North America, Bohn Aluminum, Wicks, Lowe's\n- People: James Edward Arnold\n- Places: Milan, Italy\n- Topics: motor racing seasons, corporate leadership, stock exchange listing\n\nFacts:\n- Pirelli & C. S.p.A. was listed on the Milan Stock Exchange from 1922 before later becoming an overseas subsidiary of ChemChina.\n- Pirelli & C. S.p.A. is a multinational company based in Milan, Italy.\n- The Minardi M189 was updated as the Minardi M189B for the season and was used for the first two races of the year before being replaced by the Minardi M190.\n- The Minardi M190 was powered by the Cosworth DFR V8 engine and used Pirelli tyres.\n- James Edward Arnold was one of the last presidents of Pirelli North America.\n- James Edward Arnold was also president of Bohn Aluminum and a major consultant to Wicks, which was noted for owning the Lowe's hardware chain.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
